flowchart TD
    accTitle: Browser parsing and rendering
    accDescr: HTML builds the DOM and CSS supplies styles. Together they provide the structure for layout, painting, rasterization, and compositing. JavaScript can modify the DOM and styles.
    H[HTML bytes] --> D[Parse and build the DOM]
    C[CSS bytes] --> S[Parse CSS and compute styles]
    D --> R[Build the structure for layout]
    S --> R
    R --> L[Layout: sizes and positions]
    L --> P[Paint: drawing instructions]
    P --> Z[Rasterization and compositing]
    Z --> V[Page appears on screen]
    J[JavaScript execution] --> D
    J --> S
